        <mxCell id="DqBFF7F-e4qEBxQVCtK4-23" value="Data to be stored by default:&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;position, orientation&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;thruster forces&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;resulting force&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;time stamp&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="828" width="170" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="DqBFF7F-e4qEBxQVCtK4-24" value="How to handle different frame rates?" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="420" y="810" width="220" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-2" value="Offline mode&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; Maybe more useful anyways?&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Handling different fps:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;Use ffmpeg to interpolate between images&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;temporal (mis)alignment:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- Manual alignment? That would require a &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;good preview?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- automatic alignment? I.e. estimating the &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;pos/vel from the image and try to align the &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;tracks?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;- calculate the time stamps from the video &lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;time stamp and fps?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="880" y="50" width="270" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-3" value="Online mode&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; cool af&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Handling different fps&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;always take newest of each&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: wrap; background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;temporal&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255)); text-wrap-mode: wrap;&quot;&gt;(mis)alignment:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;think about when it appears?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;resizable=1;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;movable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;labelPosition=center;verticalLabelPosition=middle;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1170" y="50" width="310" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-4" value="" style="shape=partialRectangle;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;bottom=1;right=1;left=1;top=0;fillColor=none;routingCenterX=-0.5;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="880" y="270" width="510" height="10" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-5" value="Useful for both&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;reuse the &quot;generate image from data&quot;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;reuse the data fusion&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Not useful for both&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;How to get the images/data&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Aligning the images / data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; reframing takes place after the animation has been generated???&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; Offline mode could instead interpolate the data and generate the animation at the desired frequency&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; BUT: This still does not solve the reframing issue for if the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="920" y="290" width="540" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-6" value="What about titles/information/...?&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; Logo/constant images should be able to be included&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; every other text/animation can be added later in a video editor&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="410" y="890" width="370" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-7" value="Images that &lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;change slowly:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;have an &quot;object server&quot; class that always gives the current image&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;In object server, the interpolation/hold and change/only hold/... behaviour can be implemented&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;object server contains/serves the current image data: Can be photo, video, matplotlib animation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Can have a &quot;get newest&quot; and a &quot;get step_n&quot; behaviour&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Depending on online or offline mode, the object server can first render the animation or render it on the fly&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;-&amp;gt; Maybe create a child class for animations?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;Object server can then be used for both online and offline mode" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="860" y="565" width="620" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-8" value="Need a clear way of adding different objects to the final image and position them&lt;div&gt;-&amp;gt; Does a config file make sense or is it too restrictive / not direct enough?&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="900" y="813" width="450" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-12" value="DaVinci Resolve sucks because requires GPU&lt;div&gt;Maybe best: Limit Scope to simple overlay of data, implement this myself&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="930" y="990" width="410" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="09et8kMC1PxhQDYRsZ9E-1" value="Idea: add a different filtering technique that does not need the background image" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="195" y="978" width="450" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kim30n1tNhyVVTcnEqX1-1" value="Ideas:&lt;div&gt;- for more usefulness for live debugging:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;- add way to display gridlines etc&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;- add another mode with a simple overlay (i.e. the data is simply displayed on top of the video with some transparency)&lt;/blockquote&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1110" width="690" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kim30n1tNhyVVTcnEqX1-2" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0.833;exitY=0.933;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;exitPerimeter=0;" parent="1" source="HDrXCvShkbB9lNWR8o-I-5" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
            <mxPoint x="1200" y="380" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1390" y="460" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="kim30n1tNhyVVTcnEqX1-3" value="Maybe unwanted? If there are sudden changes,&lt;div&gt;it could result in the change not being sudden, but&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;split up over two frames&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;(e.g. faulty force)&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=top;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1250" y="460" width="290" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="NupB1T_R911lVu4oHLct-1" value="- [ ] robot is still a bit &quot;before&quot; the data&lt;div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;add manual fix&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;- [ ] add live data&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;blockquote style=&quot;margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;- [ ]&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;new data streamer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;- [ ] new video streamer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;resizable=0;points=[];autosize=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1">
